---
import Container from '../Container.astro';

/*
  Pitch page section 1 — the hero statement (docs/pitch-demo-sitemap.md §4.1).

  Replaces the old email-capture "TV" hero (home/Hero.astro, commented out of
  index.astro): this site no longer collects visitor emails, and the sitemap is
  explicit that the hero carries no action at all — a CTA here competes with the
  one real CTA on the page, the ask.

  Two lines and nothing else. The environment does the rest: the nebula field and
  star layer already render behind every page from global.css and index.astro, so
  this section paints no background of its own.

  COPY STATUS, and the two lines differ:

  - The headline is the proposition as recorded in AGENTS.md ("the complete
    human experience for awakened souls, online and offline"). Not invented
    here; `copywriter` owns the final wording.
  - The subordinate line is REAL, OWNER-APPROVED COPY — "The media is the
    signal. The event is the destination." — the one line on this page exempt
    from the lorem-ipsum rule. Do not rewrite it without going back to the
    owner. It states the mechanic in the brief's own vocabulary —
    Darkness → Signal → Connection — in one line: media points, the room is
    where it ends up.

  Nothing on this screen claims anything about how many people are already in
  the network — the sitemap's named integrity risk for this section.
*/
---

<section class="pitch-hero">
  <Container>
    <div class="statement">
      <h1 class="headline">The complete human experience for awakened souls — online and offline.</h1>
      <p class="mechanic">
        The media is the <span class="signal">signal</span>. The event is the <span class="signal">destination</span>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</section>

<style>
  .pitch-hero {
    /* Full frame minus the masthead, so the first thing a funder sees is one
       sentence in an otherwise empty sky. svh (not vh) because a mobile
       browser's collapsing address bar changes vh mid-scroll, which would
       resize this block after paint. No padding-block here: the statement is
       already vertically centered inside the full-viewport min-height box, so
       section padding on top of that would just add dead space beyond the
       fold — doubled, since it stacks with Offerings' own top padding right
       below — pushing the first offering card most of a second screen down
       before a visitor sees it. The section's edge is the viewport's edge;
       Offerings' own padding-block is what creates the gap after it. */
    min-height: calc(100svh - var(--nav-height));
    display: grid;
    align-content: center;
  }

  .statement {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .headline {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    /* Measure, not a magic width: the headline holds its own line length as the
       fluid type scale grows, instead of running the full 1440px rail on desktop. */
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .mechanic {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    /* Balanced, and given enough measure to hold both sentences: at a tighter cap
       the line broke mid-clause instead of between the two sentences, which reads
       as a typo in the one line that carries the mechanic. 46ch holds both
       sentences and lets `balance` choose the sentence boundary as the break at
       every width. */
    max-width: 46ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .signal {
    color: var(--color-electric-cyan);
  }
</style>
